{"database":{"advisory-count":1338,"last-commit":"999ec89d5d3f10f20be14750ec8c2d8b44e0ac9b","last-updated":"2026-10-17T17:23:59+02:00"},"lockfile":{"dependency-count":363},"settings":{"target_arch":[],"target_os":[],"severity":null,"ignore":[],"informational_warnings":["unmaintained","unsound","notice"]},"vulnerabilities":{"found":true,"count":4,"list":[{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0204","package":"crossbeam-epoch","title":"Invalid pointer dereference in `fmt::Pointer` impl for `Atomic` and `Shared` when the underlying pointer is invalid","description":"Affected versions of `fmt::Display` dereference the underlying pointer. This causes a invalid pointer dereference e.g., when a pointer created with `Atomic::null` or `Shared::null`. `fmt::Debug` impls and pre-0.9 `fmt::Display` impls, which do not dereference pointers, are not affected by this issue.","date":"2026-07-06","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["NULL-pointer-dereference"],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/crossbeam-rs/crossbeam/pull/1276","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=0.9.20"],"unaffected":["<0.9.0"]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"crossbeam-epoch","version":"0.9.18","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"5b82ac4a3c2ca9c3460964f020e1402edd5753411d7737aa39c3714ad1b5420e","dependencies":[{"name":"crossbeam-utils","version":"0.8.21","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}},{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0367","package":"zip","title":" Insecure Preservation of SUID/SGID Bits during ZIP Extraction Leading to Potential Privilege Escalation","description":"The `zip` crate preserves privileged Unix permission bits (SUID, SGID, and sticky bits) from ZIP `external_attributes` during extraction, instead of masking them to safe permission bits. If a privileged process (for example, `root` in an installer, CI/CD pipeline, or container build) extracts an attacker-controlled ZIP archive using `ZipArchive::extract()` or the stream extraction API, files can be created as setuid-root or setgid. This behavior allows the creation of SUID/SGID files during extraction, which can lead to local privilege escalation depending on the execution environment.\n\nFor further details see: https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-vv5m-jxxh-4627","date":"2026-10-09","aliases":["GHSA-vv5m-jxxh-4627"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["privilege-escalation"],"keywords":["privilege-escalation","suid","sgid"],"cvss":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":null,"withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=9.0.0"],"unaffected":[]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"2d04a6b5381502aa6087c94c669499eb1602eb9c5e8198e534de571f7154809b","dependencies":[{"name":"crc32fast","version":"1.5.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"flate2","version":"1.1.10","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"indexmap","version":"2.14.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"memchr","version":"2.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"typed-path","version":"0.12.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"zopfli","version":"0.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}},{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0368","package":"zip","title":"zip: `ZipArchive::extract` creates symbolic links whose attacker-controlled targets are outside the destination directory","description":"In `zip` 9.0.0-pre2, `ZipArchive::extract` creates a symbolic link from an archive entry after validating only the output entry path. The link target bytes are passed directly to the platform symlink API, so a malicious archive can create an entry inside the destination that resolves to an attacker-chosen path outside it. This behavior was verified on macOS and Linux. On either platform, a subsequent application read or write through that extracted entry accesses the external target with the extracting process's permissions.\n\nFor further details see: https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-4v9h-p7m9-rh26","date":"2026-10-09","aliases":["GHSA-4v9h-p7m9-rh26"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["privilege-escalation"],"keywords":["privilege-escalation","symlink"],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":null,"withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=9.0.0"],"unaffected":[]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"2d04a6b5381502aa6087c94c669499eb1602eb9c5e8198e534de571f7154809b","dependencies":[{"name":"crc32fast","version":"1.5.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"flate2","version":"1.1.10","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"indexmap","version":"2.14.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"memchr","version":"2.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"typed-path","version":"0.12.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"zopfli","version":"0.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}},{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0369","package":"zip","title":"ZipStreamReader::extract() and ZipArchive::extract() apply Unix permissions through symlinks without confining the target","description":"`ZipStreamReader::extract()` applies Unix permissions through extracted symlinks without validating the symlink target stays within the destination\n\nFor further details see: https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-4684-h2q9-2vcp","date":"2026-10-10","aliases":["GHSA-4684-h2q9-2vcp"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["privilege-escalation"],"keywords":["privilege-escalation","symlink","permissions"],"cvss":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H","informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":null,"withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=9.0.0"],"unaffected":[]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"2d04a6b5381502aa6087c94c669499eb1602eb9c5e8198e534de571f7154809b","dependencies":[{"name":"crc32fast","version":"1.5.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"flate2","version":"1.1.10","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"indexmap","version":"2.14.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"memchr","version":"2.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"typed-path","version":"0.12.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"zopfli","version":"0.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}}]},"warnings":{"unmaintained":[{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"async-std","version":"1.13.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"2c8e079a4ab67ae52b7403632e4618815d6db36d2a010cfe41b02c1b1578f93b","dependencies":[{"name":"async-channel","version":"1.9.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"async-global-executor","version":"2.4.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"async-io","version":"2.6.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"async-lock","version":"3.4.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"async-process","version":"2.5.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"crossbeam-utils","version":"0.8.21","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-channel","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-core","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-io","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-lite","version":"2.6.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"gloo-timers","version":"0.3.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"kv-log-macro","version":"1.0.7","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"log","version":"0.4.29","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"memchr","version":"2.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"once_cell","version":"1.21.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"pin-project-lite","version":"0.2.17","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"pin-utils","version":"0.1.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"slab","version":"0.4.12","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"wasm-bindgen-futures","version":"0.4.76","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2025-0052","package":"async-std","title":"async-std has been discontinued","description":"The `async-std` has been discontinued.\n\nAlternatives:\n\n- [smol](https://crates.io/crates/smol)","date":"2025-08-24","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/async-rs/async-std","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}}],"unsound":[{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"event-listener","version":"5.4.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"e13b66accf52311f30a0db42147dadea9850cb48cd070028831ae5f5d4b856ab","dependencies":[{"name":"concurrent-queue","version":"2.5.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"parking","version":"2.2.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"pin-project-lite","version":"0.2.17","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0221","package":"event-listener","title":"`event-listener` allows `!Send` tags to cross thread boundaries via `StackSlot`","description":"Affected versions of `event-listener` unconditionally implement `Send` and\n`Sync` for `StackSlot<'_, T>`, the stack-allocated listener type created\nby the `listener!` macro.\n\nThis allows a `!Send` tag type set via `Event::with_tag` to be moved to\nanother thread and accessed via `StackSlot::wait`, causing a data race in safe\ncode.","date":"2026-07-13","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["memory-corruption","thread-safety"],"keywords":["concurrency"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/smol-rs/event-listener/pull/163","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[">=5.4.2"],"unaffected":["<5.1.0"]}},{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"memmap2","version":"0.5.10","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"83faa42c0a078c393f6b29d5db232d8be22776a891f8f56e5284faee4a20b327","dependencies":[{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.186","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0186","package":"memmap2","title":"Unchecked pointer offset in crate `memmap2`","description":"Affected versionf of `memmap2` did not perform enough validation on the `offset` and `len` parameters of\n`Mmap::[unchecked_]advise_range()`,\n`MmapMut::[unchecked_]advise_ranage()`\nand `MmapMut::flush[_async]_range()`.\n\nThis can cause undefined behavior due to invalid values being passed to [`pointer::offset()`] and [`pointer::add()`]\nwhen passing an out-of-bounds range to any of the affected functions.\n\nThe flaw was corrected in commit [`cee7cf0`] and released in version `0.9.11`.\n\nThe invalid pointer is not dereferenced,\nbut it is passed to the `madvise` and `msync` syscalls and their Windows equivalents.\n\n[`pointer::offset()`]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.offset-1\n[`pointer::add()`]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/primitive.pointer.html#method.add-1\n[`cee7cf0`] https://github.com/RazrFalcon/memmap2-rs/pull/170/changes/cee7cf03a9ee095982a3c37b7aac8e3f68f1a00c","date":"2026-06-20","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["pointer-arithmetic","out-of-bounds"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":["https://github.com/RazrFalcon/memmap2-rs/pull/170"],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/RazrFalcon/memmap2-rs/issues/169","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":{"arch":[],"os":[],"functions":{"memmap2::Mmap::advise_range":[">=0.5.9","<0.9.11"],"memmap2::Mmap::unchecked_advise_range":[">=0.8.0","<0.9.11"],"memmap2::MmapMut::advise_range":[">=0.5.9","<0.9.11"],"memmap2::MmapMut::flush_async_range":["<0.9.11"],"memmap2::MmapMut::flush_range":["<0.9.11"],"memmap2::MmapMut::unchecked_advise_range":[">=0.8.0","<0.9.11"]}},"versions":{"patched":[">=0.9.11"],"unaffected":[]}}]}}
